{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_tppn4oj4oaj5puvzibadxla7ketbmr425jmf65diked23neeb26q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — **all four phases pass**. `run_all.sh` reports `ALL CHECKS PASSED`.\n\n## Result\n\nThe Rust translation of this `stb_ds.h`-derived library is **behaviourally identical to the C** across 88 differential tests. `cargo check` was already clean; **no divergence was found in `src/lib.rs`, so no fixes to the translation were needed.**\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` diff empty, 0 undefined non-libc | ✅ 16/16 both directions |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row (C1–C65) | ✅ 55 tests |\n| Binary stdout comparison | ✅ vacuous — neither project builds an executable (asserted, not assumed) |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row (E1–E48) | ✅ 33 tests |\n| All feature combos | ✅ no `[features]` table ⇒ default + `--no-default-features`, both green |\n\n## Three real defects found — all in the *verification infrastructure*, and each caused a false result\n\n1. **`cargo test` never rebuilds a `cdylib`.** The suite was `dlopen`ing a stale `.so` and reporting green for sources it had never executed. Caught only because I mutation-tested; `assert_so_is_fresh` in `tests/common/mod.rs` now panics if the `.so` is older than `src/`.\n2. **`stbds_hash_seed` is process-global** and `dlopen` of one path returns one object, so `cargo test`'s parallelism let tests advance each other's seed. `both()` now holds a process-wide mutex.\n3. Three C properties make naive byte comparison bogus — each cost a false failure: `hmput_key` writes only `keysize` bytes (the rest is caller scratch = raw `realloc` garbage); `temp_key` is left **uninitialised** by `stbds_make_hash_index` and never cleared (dangling after a strdup delete); `SH_DEFAULT` stores the caller's pointer verbatim.\n\n## Suite validated by mutation testing\n\n19 single-line mutations injected into `src/lib.rs`: **17/17 non-equivalent ones caught**. The 2 misses are provably *equivalent mutants*, not gaps — `min_cap < 4 → < 5` (branch body assigns `4` either way) and `hmdel_key`'s `ptr::null_mut() → a` (that arm only runs inside `if a.is_null()`).\n\n## Notable C behaviours replicated and pinned\n\n- `__assert_fail` is a live import — CMake sets no build type, so **every `STBDS_ASSERT` is active in C**. This makes `mode >= 2` + `old_index != final_index` in `hmdel_key` genuinely *abort* (it hashes raw pointer bytes as a string), so E15/E18 are tested only in their non-aborting shapes, with the reason documented rather than silently skipped.\n- The `int` sign-extension in siphash's word assembly (`d[3] << 24`), versus `unsigned char` zero-extension in `hash_string` — opposite conventions, both correct, both pinned.\n- `stbds_shmode_func` truncates `mode` to `unsigned char` (610 int values swept); out-of-enum `string.mode` silently falls into the raw-`memcpy` arm even for string-mode puts.\n- `elemsize*min_cap` wrapping to 0 so `realloc` gets only the 32-byte header while `capacity` records an astronomical value.\n\nTwo `ERRORS.md` rows are unreachable-by-construction rather than tested: E35 (`hash < 2` needs inverting siphash — 200k probes recorded as a negative result) and E3 (`arrfreef(NULL)` = `free((void*)-32)`, which would kill the test process). `c_src/` is unmodified apart from the `build/` directory."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":737,"cache_read_input_tokens":291793,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":737,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6cd1d22-8154-44e8-9cdb-2db26a93be9c","uuid":"a9dc1e0a-c570-42ea-a33d-1d5a213084f9","timestamp":"2026-09-05T06:38:05.381Z"}
